# Environment for the Helm API (local development).
#
# Quick start (1Password):
#   1. cp apps/api/.env.local.example apps/api/.env.local
#   2. Edit .env.local — set HELM_KNOWLEDGE_REPO_PATH, HELM_DATA_DIR, GITHUB_TOKEN
#   3. pnpm sync-env          # resolves op:// refs from .env.template → .env
#   4. pnpm dev
#
# Bun reads `.env` from apps/api/ (the API process CWD), not the repo root.
#
# Files:
#   .env.template       — committed; op:// secret references for 1Password
#   .env.local.example  — committed; template for machine-specific values
#   .env.local          — gitignored; your paths + optional token override
#   .env                — gitignored; generated by `pnpm sync-env` (do not edit by hand)

# --- Secrets (in .env.template, resolved by sync-env) ---
# LINEAR_API_KEY=op://…
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=op://…

# --- Local (in .env.local) ---
# HELM_KNOWLEDGE_REPO_PATH=/absolute/path/to/knowledge-repo
# HELM_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/helm/apps/api/data
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_…  # or use output of `gh auth token`
